on"},{"id":"source-question:3e140b31c328834eab5600d365ad586ddb747b81409fb1b2a3ce5d989576c9b4","title":"The polar construction separates angular circulation from a radial potential force that can balance it. A general radial kinetic function permits curved field space, while the numerical examples use a flat plane.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0057"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:3e31780d7054e9c9bcb05f992f19a51f70bbbc8450e59a9ea2201b251deeae82","title":"Does adding the non-minimal scalar-curvature coupling preserve interacting Yukawa fixed points associated with predictions or upper bounds for fermion masses?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0057"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:3e47f269b12cc12ce9394273690bdfb747e9bc028340c67b5a2cdadbc2de6cca","title":"When does identifying the ultraviolet cutoff of a logarithmically divergent axion EFT loop with f_a reproduce a complete QCD axion model, particularly for K⁺→π⁺a? Can a renormalizable model realize the large logarithm without additional states below the PQ scale?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0061"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:3ea5d2c430fc463436dd8d0b4d38f429f5b2a69209d9a94593d5823549b69fac","title":"How reliably do R-symmetry field counts predict supersymmetric versus SUSY-breaking Wess–Zumino models when special R-charge assignments can evade genericity, and how can a finite model dataset quantify these exceptions?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0075"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:3ef97fab72b145fad3530e01917f293b0833898884699ae73b8ff295b7bad275","title":"How does decomposition organize condensation defects, explain multiplicities in their fusion, and motivate additional defects whose worldvolume higher-form gauging selects universes?","connectionCount":1,"detail"